      },
      {
        "kind": "text",
        "text": "Level is anchored on the latest two observations. Momentum receives no extrapolation: May-to-June declined 1.1025 percentage points, while earlier changes reversed sharply. February and April are treated as possible cohort, processing, or reporting effects rather than evidence of a permanent level change; their causes are unverified, so both remain in uncertainty calibration. No policy adjustment is applied without fetched evidence of an Idaho-specific change."
